<title>SWEDEN: FORECAST - Swedish Match '96 profit seen down 3 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Swedish Match '96 profit seen down 3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish Match was expected to post a pre-tax profit of 1.53 billion crowns for 1996 against 1.58 billion in 1995, according to a Reuter poll of eight analysts on Monday.</p>
<p>Forecasts varied between 1.50 billion crowns and 1.60 billion crowns.</p>
<p>Analysts forecast pre-tax profit in 1997 would rise to 1.68 billion crowns.</p>
<p>Analysts interviewed for the poll were from James Capel, Fiba Nordic, Swedbank, Aros, Carnegie, Nordiska, Hagstromer &amp; Qviberg and Enskilda.</p>
<p>Swedish Match is due to release its 1996 report on March 3.</p>
<p>    (Mln SKR)	     AVG	    RANGE     ANALYSTS</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit 1996    1,530	  1,496-1,604	 8</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit 1997    1,683	  1,541-1,760	 8</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit 1998    1,815	  1,587-1,985	 8</p>
<p> Earnings/share (Skr)    2.32	   2.20-2.47	  7</p>
<p> Dividend (Skr)	    1.04	   1.00-1.10	  8</p>
<p>-- Olle Lindstrom, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1015</p>
